  "prediction": "**Implementing Telework to Reduce Office Space: Challenges and Opportunities**\n\nThe Government Accountability Office (GAO) conducted a study to examine how civilian Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Act agencies use telework to reduce office space and increase efficiency. The study found that most agencies have a telework program in place, but many face challenges in using telework as a strategic space-planning tool.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n* 23 civilian CFO Act agencies reported using telework to reduce or optimize office space, with 15 agencies incorporating telework into their space-planning policies.\n* Agencies reported using telework to reduce space needs, increase operational efficiency, and lower real estate costs.\n* GSA, OJP, and CDC were identified as agencies that have successfully implemented telework to reduce space, with GSA achieving a 30% reduction in space through telework and hoteling.\n* Challenges faced by agencies include human capital issues, such as negotiating workspace changes and managing organizational change, as well as difficulty measuring cost savings and assessing the impact of telework on space planning.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n* The GSA Administrator should develop guidance on using telework as a strategic space-planning tool, including how to measure cost savings and assess the impact of telework on space planning.\n* The GSA Administrator should complete the Workplace Investment and Feasibility Tool, a tool designed to help agencies quantify the benefits and costs of telework, and make it available to federal agencies.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nImplementing telework can be an effective way for agencies to reduce office space and increase efficiency. However, agencies face challenges in using telework as a strategic space-planning tool, including human capital issues and difficulty measuring cost savings. To address these challenges, the GSA Administrator should develop guidance and tools to support agencies in using telework to reduce space and increase efficiency.",
